---
source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/cases/pending-documentation.rs
expression: "stdout(&env, &listed)"
---
# instrukt docs index: snippet ids with their descriptions
# Filter with --domain <acme> (repeatable), --areas <principle|concept|policy|procedure|design|spec|adr>, --third-party, --target <slug>, --project <slug>
# Source of project demo: [TMP]/demo/docs/project/ — published commit [SHA] — remote none

acme/concept/old: A concept build-it retires. (superseded by: build-it)
acme/policy/reworked: A live policy with a next version. (superseded by: build-it)
acme/spec/fresh: A new contract build-it delivers. (delivered by: build-it)
acme/spec/later: A new contract other-work delivers. (delivered by: other-work)
acme/spec/live: A live contract with pending additions. (superseded by: build-it, other-work)

# Read the snippets you need: instrukt docs get <id> [<id>…]
# Pending documentation is flagged, never hidden: `(delivered by: <slugs>)` marks a snippet not yet delivered, `(superseded by: <slugs>)` a live snippet with pending changes. `instrukt docs get` reads the current contract; `--target <slug>` on `index` and `get` shows the documentation as that todo will deliver it.
